<div class="stickiness-def">
  <p class="stickiness-lede">
    In
    <a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US1706491A/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
      >1929, the inventor of stick food patented</a
    >
    the idea of &ldquo;a food product <strong>on a stick for a handle</strong>.&rdquo; In this
    challenge we hope to live up to his vision. Our last category is a bit nebulous but still
    crucial; it evaluates how well the stick functions as an integral part of the dish.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The stick is the handle</strong> &mdash; no plate, no fork, no second hand needed
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The stick holds</strong> &mdash; it keeps everything together from the first bite to
      the last.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No stick, no dish</strong> &mdash; take the stick away and it just wouldn't be the
      same
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="stickiness-verdict">
    Use your best judgment &mdash; score 1 to 5 on how well the entry lives up to the essence of the
    stick.
  </p>
</div>
